From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] media: mediatek: add an MT6797 stateless HEVC decoder
 prototype

The MT6797 VDEC has no firmware: the CPU programs its registers for every
picture. Expose it as a V4L2 stateless memory-to-memory decoder: HEVC
slices in (frame-based, Annex-B), MM21 frames out (two planes).

Per picture the driver walks the first slice header through the decoder
bit reader, programs the picture, reference and buffer registers from the
HEVC controls and the DPB, lets the hardware parse reference-list
modification and prediction weights itself, and issues one start; the
hardware decodes every slice of the picture. Without an IOMMU the decoder
uses physical addresses: LARB1 per-port translation is cleared after each
power-up and buffers are allocated below 4 GiB.

The programming was reconstructed from observed register traces and is
written independently. Main profile, 8-bit 4:2:0 only; 10-bit, other chroma
formats and slice-based decoding are rejected. Validated offline against
60 recorded pictures; not yet run on hardware.

Prototype, not for upstream submission in this form.
